WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.966
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.966 --> 00:00:06.300
Here's a fun logic puzzle. Four friends

00:00:06.433 --> 00:00:11.066
claim they had been wrongly imprisoned
and they are just mere logicians,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.066
and they have been confused for criminals.

00:00:14.066 --> 00:00:16.400
The warden says if you are in fact

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.766
logicians, I'm
going to give you a chance to prove it.

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:22.833
So he lines up
the four logicians as follows.

00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:27.666
We have 1, 2, 3
all facing forward, then a brick wall.

00:00:27.733 --> 00:00:31.866
And then on the other side of the brick
wall is logician 4.

00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:34.466
The warden says, “I'm going to place

00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:37.933
2 blue hats
and 2 red hats on the 4 of you.”

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.000
They all know these rules.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.700
They're only allowed
to look in front of them.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.766
There's no cheating.

00:00:43.766 --> 00:00:45.766
They're not allowed
to take their hats off.

00:00:45.766 --> 00:00:47.866
They're not allowed to talk to each other.

00:00:47.866 --> 00:00:49.900
And they're not allowed to do anything
else.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:55.666
They have to figure out the answer
using pure logical reasoning.

00:00:55.766 --> 00:00:58.766
The warden
says, “I’m going to give you some time.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.033
If any one of you can state the color
of your hat with certainty,

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:07.066
I will let you all out for free.”

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:10.933
Being perfect logicians, none of them
will speak out of turn and just guess.

00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:15.033
They will only speak
if they know the answer for sure.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.866
So the question is can
the four logicians be freed?

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:21.233
And how would they do it?

00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:24.400
Pause the video
if you'd like to give this problem a try.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.133
And when you're ready, keep
watching to learn

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:34.833
how to solve this problem.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.866
So how can we work it out?

00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:41.200
First, logician
3 only looks at a brick wall.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:44.566
So there's no information
that the third person could have.

00:01:44.666 --> 00:01:48.500
There's no way this person
could shout out with certainty.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.300
The same thing is true for logician 4.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.500
The logician only sees a brick wall
and doesn't have any information.

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:59.433
So 4 is not going
to shout out any answers.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.866
Now, each of them is thinking

00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:04.866
there are 2 blue hats and 2 red hats.

00:02:04.966 --> 00:02:09.700
So there are, of course, 4 choose 2,
which is 4 factorial over 2 factorial,

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:14.800
2 factorial, equals 6
different ways for the warden to arrange

00:02:14.866 --> 00:02:19.166
2 blue hats
and 2 red hats on the 4 of them.

00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:22.000
So they start thinking,
what are the possibilities?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.433
It could be red, red, blue, blue, 
red, blue, red, blue, 

00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:29.366
red, blue, blue, red, 
blue, blue, red, red,

00:02:29.433 --> 00:02:35.266
blue, red, blue, red 
or blue, red, red, blue.

00:02:35.366 --> 00:02:37.766
Now logician 2 sees

00:02:37.766 --> 00:02:40.933
a red hat on the third person.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:44.666
So logician 2 looks
at which possibilities have a blue

00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:50.300
hat on the third option and says
these cannot be the possible arrangements.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.800
So we are down to 3 possibilities.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.900
Now, logician 1
is also thinking the same thing

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.800
because logician 1 can see the hats
on logicians 2 and 3.

00:03:01.866 --> 00:03:06.566
So logician 1 not only knows
they're down to these 3 possibilities,

00:03:06.633 --> 00:03:11.366
but logician 1 also knows
that there's a blue hat and a red hat.

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:14.400
So that leaves only 2 possibilities

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.100
But still in each of these possibilities,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:21.000
logician 1 says, I don't know
if I'm wearing a red hat or blue hat

00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:25.833
because either one is possible
in these two possibilities,

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.300
And that's the clue!

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.500
So after a while, logician 2

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:35.100
knows that logician 1 is confused.

00:03:35.166 --> 00:03:38.366
Now, if logician 1 had seen

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.500
two red hats,
that is red hats on 2 and 3,

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:47.333
logician 1
would know that his hat was blue.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.400
But since logician 1 is confused,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.766
logician 2
says this possibility cannot be true.

00:03:54.866 --> 00:03:57.600
So we are down to 2 possibilities

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.400
And logician 2
thinks in each of these possibilities.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.900
There is a blue
hat in the second position.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.966
Therefore, logician 2 says,
I know my hat is blue!

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:14.166
And all 4
of the logicians get set free.

00:04:14.233 --> 00:04:17.033
What an incredible logic puzzle!

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:20.033
Thanks for making us
one of the best communities on YouTube.

